<div class="wrap inside"><a class="breadcrumb" href="@root/work/">Selected work</a><section class="book-profile"><div class="book-display tall"><img src="@root/assets/aranyani-cover.webp" alt="Araṇyani, original National Book Trust cover" width="350" height="547"></div><div>{{label('Kannada historical fiction')}}<h1>Araṇyani</h1><p class="kannada-name" lang="kn">ಅರಣ್ಯನಿ</p><p class="deck">Set in the rainforests of the Western Ghats, Araṇyani follows communities defending their land and traditions under British rule.</p><p>In writing the novel, I drew on accounts of local resistance, the martial art of Kalarippayattu, regional traditions of worship and teachings from the Upanishads.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="{{site.book}}">{{icon('reader')}} Publisher’s catalogue</a><a class="text-link" href="https://www.amazon.in/dp/9354916414">Find the book</a></div></div></section>
<div class="essay-grid"><section><h2>Publication and reception</h2><p>PM-YUVA selected 75 young authors from more than 16,000 proposals submitted across 22 languages. Araṇyani was the only Kannada title published by National Book Trust under that first programme.</p><p>National Book Trust launched the book at the New Delhi World Book Fair alongside the other PM-YUVA titles. My Kannada author profile reports sales of approximately 40,000 copies.</p></section><aside class="side-note"><span class="kicker">Author’s note · Kannada</span><h2 lang="kn">ಕೃತಿಯ ಬಗ್ಗೆ ಲೇಖಕರ ಮಾತು</h2><a class="text-link" href="@root/blog/aranyani-authors-note/">Read the author’s note</a></aside></div><figure class="literary-meeting">
